# Diagrams — the Mermaid dialect

`context/instructions/diagram-mermaid.md` is the format contract for a diagram
written in **Mermaid**: a fenced `mermaid` block inside a Markdown document, so
the diagram stays diffable in git and readable by an agent without image
rendering. Read it together with `context/instructions/diagram.md` (the doctrine:
type, layout, honesty) and `context/instructions/development.md` (the process
contract).

## Nothing is dropped

The diagram is the document: a renderer draws it, it never rewrites it. A
diagram that only survives as a rendered image has lost its source, and every
edit has to start over.

## The block

A diagram is a fenced code block tagged `mermaid`, embedded in the document that
owns it:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A[request] --> B[service]
  B --> C[(store)]
```

It is not a separate asset file: the diagram lives next to the prose it
explains, so the two move together. Authored SVG assets are a different lane
(`context/instructions/vector-svg.md`).

## Type keywords

Map the reader's question (see `diagram.md`) to a Mermaid keyword:

| Question | Keyword |
|---|---|
| steps and decisions over time | `flowchart` |
| messages exchanged in order | `sequenceDiagram` |
| states and transitions | `stateDiagram-v2` |
| data between stores and processes | `flowchart` with data-shaped nodes |
| entities and relations | `erDiagram` |
| parts and boundaries of a system | `flowchart` with subgraphs |
| a schedule over time | `gantt` |

## Portable subset

Write the standard Mermaid the project's renderer draws. Prefer the plain
constructs — node shapes, arrows with short labels, a subgraph for a boundary —
over renderer-specific tweaks.

## Anti-patterns

- Styling-only changes: a theme or colour tweak is not a diagram improvement.
- `classDef` sprawl: a class per node is a stylesheet, not a diagram.
- Relying on automatic layout: place by connection (`diagram.md`); never accept a
  default that scrambles the reading order.
- Beautifying the renderer: a prettier theme does not add information.

## Label semantics

A relationship label carries meaning (action, protocol, direction, async,
cross-boundary). Keep it short; never delete it to make room.

## Where a diagram lives

- Embedded in the owning document (an architecture page, an analysis, a worklog).
- `.map.md` (mind maps) and `.slide.md` (decks) are their own lanes, not this
  one.
- Every diagram keeps its source block; a canonical export strips
  presentation-only marks.

## Boundary

- Doctrine (type, layout, honesty) defers to `context/instructions/diagram.md`.
- Authored SVG assets defer to `context/instructions/vector-svg.md`.
- Tool choice, install and code defer to
  `context/instructions/development.md`.
- This module names no rendering tool and no exporter.
